{
  "version": 1,
  "purpose": "Expand the live 720-region world through East Africa using persistent physical regions. Modern country boundaries are source geometry only and are deliberately allowed to disappear when gameplay regions are clustered.",
  "targetExistingRegionCount": 720,
  "principles": [
    "Modern borders are raw geometry sources, not gameplay borders.",
    "Cluster source units across modern frontiers when they belong to the same durable physical zone.",
    "Prefer highlands, rifts, lakes, river basins, escarpments, coasts, savannahs and caravan corridors as long-lived region identities.",
    "Keep the Ethiopian coffee-origin highlands geographically explicit rather than unlocking coffee through a modern state tag.",
    "Maintain enough coastal detail for Red Sea and Indian Ocean trade without reproducing every modern district."
  ],
